  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrating Peacebuilding and Social Cohesion in Refugee Management in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen peacebuilding and social cohesion among refugees and host communities in Kenya&#x2019;s Dadaab refugee camps. It aligns with national and county policy frameworks, particularly the Shirika Plan and the Garissa Integrated Socio-Economic Development Plan (GISEDP). The Shirika Plan, set for launch in 2024, seeks to transform refugee camps into integrated settlements, promoting sustainable services and economic opportunities. Despite past efforts, tensions persist due to reso</narrative>
  </description>
